    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe owner-creation endpoint is `POST /api/owners` \u2192 `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`, which delegates each business rule to `ClinicService` and returns `409 CONFLICT` on violation (existing pattern for duplicate telephone / household conflicts). I followed that same structure for the new per-city capacity rule:\n\n- **`OwnerRepository`** already exposed `countByCityIgnoreCase(city)` \u2014 reused it, no repository change needed.\n- **`ClinicService`** \u2014 added the business predicate `boolean isCityAtCapacity(String city)`.\n- **`ClinicServiceImpl`** \u2014 implemented it as `countByCityIgnoreCase(city) >= CITY_CAPACITY`, with `CITY_CAPACITY = 50` as a named constant, `@Transactional(readOnly = true)` like the sibling query methods.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 added a guard that returns `409 CONFLICT` when `isCityAtCapacity(owner.getCity())`, placed alongside the existing conflict checks before the owner is saved.\n\nLogic lives where it belongs: the count query in the repository, the \"at capacity\" business decision in the service, and the HTTP status mapping in the controller \u2014 no duplication and no method turned into a catch-all.",
